    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d769">

                <pb facs="0878" n="785" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg785"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.404/1509a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Daniels</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-04T14:00:00-05:00">February 4, 1935—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. Borah resolution<anchor n="40" xml:id="d769-f1"/> contains allegations that
                    “American citizens of the Christian faiths have been outraged and reviled, their
                    homes <pb facs="0879" n="786" xml:id="pg786"/> invaded, their civil rights
                    abridged, and their lives placed in jeopardy” and further that “cruelties and
                    brutalities have accompanied the campaign of the Mexican Government against the
                    profession and practice of religious beliefs by our nationals.”</p>
                <p>Telegraph immediately whether Embassy has any information tending to substantiate
                    these allegations of mistreatment of or denial of rights to American citizens in
                    Mexico. Should any such information come to your attention in the future you
                    should report it promptly to the Department by telegram instructing all Consuls
                    to do likewise.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
